	<!-- Core Architectural Profile -->
	<div class="space-y-8 font-mono text-sm">

		<!-- ARCHITECT MANIFESTO / EXECUTIVE SUMMARY -->
		<section>
			<h3 class="text-[#34d399] text-xs uppercase tracking-widest font-bold mb-3">00. System Philosophy & Abstraction Depth</h3>
			<div class="bg-[#1e293b] border border-[#334155] p-5 rounded font-sans text-sm text-[#cbd5e1] leading-relaxed space-y-4">
				<p>
					Modern infrastructure engineering is plagued by <span class="text-[#f472b6] font-mono">leaky abstractions</span>. Writing high-level Infrastructure as Code (IaC) without understanding the physical layer is like trying to tune a high-performance engine without knowing how internal combustion works. The best racecar drivers are intimately familiar with mechanical engineering; similarly, true platform orchestration requires an absolute perspective that spans from cloud-native software frameworks down to the bare metal.
				</p>
				<p>
					My expertise blends modern software methodologies with a core-principle mastery of every layer of the technology stack. Having physically worked inside data centers, mounted bare metal, carved out SAN/NAS storage planes, and routed IP packets through physical switches as the industry evolved, I don't just consume API wrappers—I understand the structural constraints beneath them. 
				</p>
				<p>
					Whether configuring memory allocations, optimizing hypervisor layouts, or debugging complex state synchronization sagas across distributed systems, this holistic perspective allows me to build architectures that are deterministic, deeply secure, and structurally immune to unexpected infrastructural friction.
				</p>
			</div>
		</section>
		
		<!-- 01. SYSTEMS & TOOLING MATRIX -->
		<section>
			<h3 class="text-[#34d399] text-xs uppercase tracking-widest font-bold mb-3">01. Core Systems & Tooling Matrix</h3>
			<pre class="bg-[#1e293b] p-4 rounded text-[#cbd5e1] border border-[#334155] leading-relaxed text-xs overflow-x-auto">
[CLOUD PLATFORMS]     AWS // Azure // GCP // OpenStack // Hybrid Bare-Metal
[INFRASTRUCTURE/IaC]   Terraform // Bicep // CloudFormation // Puppet // Ansible
[CONTAINERIZATION]     Kubernetes (EKS, AKS, GKE) // Docker // Helm
[AUTOMATION / CI-CD]   GitHub Actions // GitLab CI // Jenkins // AWS CodePipeline
[SCRIPTING CHANNELS]   Python // Bash // PowerShell // Node.js
[SYSTEMS / HYPERVISOR] Linux (RHEL, Ubuntu) // Windows Server // VMware vSphere
[NETWORKING & SEC]     Zero-Trust Architecture // IAM // VPC Topology // API Isolation
[DATA & AUTOMATION]    AI/ML Data Pipelines // Vector DBs // RAG Systems // HPC Scheduling</pre>
		</section>

